3}^{k}>1+{2}^{k}\n$$\n\nThen, we move on to the **inductive step**: We must show that $P(k)⇒P(k+1).$ We start by writing down $P(k+1).$\n\n**Inductive Step**: We're required to prove that\n\n$$\n{3}^{k+1}>1+{2}^{k+1}.\n$$\n\nThe inductive step is where most of the work lies. The idea is to rewrite the left-hand side of this inequality using the inductive hypothesis and apply algebraic techniques to show that this is greater than the right-hand side.\n\nOnce we've shown that $P(k)⇒P(k+1),$ the proof is complete, and we state our **conclusion**.\n\n**Conclusion**: Therefore, ${3}^{n}>1+{2}^{n}$ for all $n\\ge 2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418775 #edb/ref 1080 "(k+1)^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418775 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418775 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "011977f1-82e7-5433-ae62-98ea6532bb6e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418776 #edb/ref 1080 "2(2k+1)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418776 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418776 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "01300c2d-9bb1-5daa-add3-114170c3dc97" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418777 #edb/ref 1080 "{k}^{2}+3{k}^{2}+5k+2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418777 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418777 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "01e6e32a-d416-5772-96d6-916097367996" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418778 #edb/ref 1080 "{k}^{2}+k" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418778 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418778 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "020fbca0-f27d-5e03-8e55-2b6786cd577f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418779 #edb/ref 1080 "3{k}^{2}+6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418779 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418779 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "063632df-9b00-55d5-895a-5a45857d917d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418780 #edb/ref 1080 "(k+2)^{2}+2{k}^{2}+2k-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418780 #edb/ref 1082 #ed